# Build context hygiene: none of this may end up in the image.
#
# The important lines are the last group: runtime config and secrets are mounted at run time, and
# copying them into a layer would (a) leak .env into an inspectable image and (b) freeze a snapshot
# of this particular host's services into an image meant to run on any Docker host.

# git + tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.arena
.cache
.nox
.vscode
.idea
*.swp

# build output and installed deps (rebuilt inside the image)
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
coverage
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# runtime state — always a bind mount, never a COPY
data
config
.env
.env.*
config/.env
config/.env.*
**/.env
**/*.env
config/backups
config/icons
config/backgrounds

# anything key-shaped, wherever it is parked in the tree
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.secret
secrets
secrets.*

# source of truth for these exclusions / not needed at runtime
docs
test
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
